Python (ryoku/shell/quickshell/shell/modules/bar/barstyles/python/)

Python is a Ryoku bar style based on Serpantinum, created by ilyamiro and
contributors (https://github.com/ilyamiro/serpantinum). It is a modified
version: the QML surfaces are ported near-verbatim, while the data plane runs
through Ryoku's window-manager seam, settings daemon, palette and services,
and the launcher, clipboard, wallpaper, lock, screenshot and update surfaces
are Ryoku's own and are not part of this port.

This port tracks Serpantinum at commit cfdd810, past 2.2.12. Ryoku carries the
upstream bar registry, orientation-aware faces, shader effects, liquid-glass
material, settings guide, popups and widget-face library. It leaves out
Serpantinum's launcher, clipboard, wallpaper, lock, capture, notification
server, policy agent, idle service, updater, first-run flow, compositor
trackers and desktop-widget host because Ryoku provides those facilities.

